"subs": [
{
"t": 1.55,
"dur": 1.349,
"text": "Easy, son. It's hot."
},
{
"t": 4.749,
"dur": 1.184,
"text": "Wait. Don't ask yet."
},
{
"t": 6.183,
"dur": 2.897,
"text": "An old woman. Her head. In a rice cooker. Live."
},
{
"t": 9.33,
"dur": 2.931,
"text": "Want to know why? Let's go back three months. I'll tell you."
},
{
"t": 12.761,
"dur": 3.874,
"text": "Three months ago, my son started a channel. He called it Dinner with Mom."
},
{
"t": 16.885,
"dur": 2.964,
"text": "Every meal: braised fish, crab soup, fried eggs."
},
{
"t": 20.099,
"dur": 2.785,
"text": "Three million viewers. They cried. They sent money."
},
{
"t": 23.134,
"dur": 4.838,
"text": "The second he turned it off, he packed it up. Into a plastic bag, back to the restaurant."
},
{
"t": 28.222,
"dur": 1.542,
"text": "I got plain rice porridge."
},
{
"t": 30.014,
"dur": 3.697,
"text": "He isn't evil. He's in debt to an app. His phone buzzes all day."
},
{
"t": 33.962,
"dur": 4.522,
"text": "I'm not mad. I've got a secret too. Every night, I sneak out for a late meal."
},
{
"t": 38.634,
"dur": 0.898,
"text": "Just my head."
},
{
"t": 40.132,
"dur": 8.646,
"text": "I'm a ma lai — a head-flying ghost. At two a.m., my head lifts off and flies out the window. I put it back before the rooster crows."
},
{
"t": 49.028,
"dur": 3.074,
"text": "Flying around town is hard now. Cameras everywhere."
},
{
"t": 52.351,
"dur": 5.604,
"text": "What do I eat? Leftover braised fish from the trash. I split it with a tabby cat. She's pregnant."
},
{
"t": 58.205,
"dur": 1.687,
"text": "My grandma gave me one rule."
},
{
"t": 60.293,
"dur": 3.477,
"text": "Listen, son. When I'm asleep, don't pull the blanket up to my neck."
},
{
"t": 64.019,
"dur": 1.427,
"text": "Mom, that's just superstition."
},
{
"t": 65.696,
"dur": 1.467,
"text": "He laughed. Then forgot."
},
{
"t": 67.663,
"dur": 4.421,
"text": "Then he had a new idea: stream while I slept. Eight hours of healing with Mom."
},
{
"t": 72.334,
"dur": 2.118,
"text": "At two oh seven, the comments blew up."
},
{
"t": 75.652,
"dur": 3.187,
"text": "The next day, he added a light. Pointed right at the window."
},
{
"t": 79.089,
"dur": 4.722,
"text": "That night, the camera caught four seconds. Four seconds of a blanket, flat at the neck."
},
{
"t": 84.812,
"dur": 7.742,
"text": "The internet went nuts. People zoomed in on every pixel. A feng shui guy sold ma lai-proof bracelets, half off."
},
{
"t": 92.803,
"dur": 2.929,
"text": "People fear ghosts. Ghosts fear the algorithm."
},
{
"t": 96.332,
"dur": 6.172,
"text": "Only Mrs. Hanh next door stayed quiet. She came over, sat down, and looked at me for a long time."
},
{
"t": 102.754,
"dur": 1.476,
"text": "Granny Tu. Be careful."
},
{
"t": 104.48,
"dur": 6.443,
"text": "She didn't mean my son should be careful. She meant me. Turns out, someone can know you're a ghost and still worry about you."
},
{
"t": 111.523,
"dur": 3.337,
"text": "That night, he put a camera on top of the cabinet. The title:"
},
{
"t": 116.959,
"dur": 4.409,
"text": "At two fifteen, he nodded off. Nine thousand people stayed awake for him."
},
{
"t": 121.618,
"dur": 1.28,
"text": "And my head got lighter."
},
{
"t": 123.698,
"dur": 2.694,
"text": "His phone buzzed. He woke up. Looked at the bed."
},
{
"t": 126.642,
"dur": 2.087,
"text": "The floral blanket. Flat at the neck."
},
{
"t": 130.329,
"dur": 6.686,
"text": "He didn't scream. He didn't dare lift the blanket. His hands shook as he pulled it over me. Up to my neck. All the way."
},
{
"t": 137.266,
"dur": 5.182,
"text": "Outside the window, I saw it all. My son had tucked me in for the first time in three months."
},
{
"t": 142.696,
"dur": 1.214,
"text": "And I couldn't get back."
},
{
"t": 144.911,
"dur": 4.696,
"text": "I nearly dropped my water pipe. Two hours till the rooster crowed. Where'd she hide?"
},
{
"t": 149.857,
"dur": 2.946,
"text": "Where's dark and warm, and just the right size for a head?"
},
{
"t": 153.052,
"dur": 0.943,
"text": "The rice cooker."
},
{
"t": 154.496,
"dur": 9.443,
"text": "Sunlight makes me melt. But no sun gets inside a rice cooker. Fifty years as a ma lai, and my first night sleeping in one. Warmer than a blanket."
},
{
"t": 164.638,
"dur": 8.905,
"text": "Seven a.m. The stream was still on. Three hundred thousand viewers. And he did what he did every morning: opened the cooker to rinse the rice."
},
{
"t": 174.643,
"dur": 1.349,
"text": "Easy, son. It's hot."
},
{
"t": 179.542,
"dur": 4.383,
"text": "Tung! Who taught you to wrap an old woman up like that? Your mom's gonna suffocate!"
},
{
"t": 184.176,
"dur": 3.784,
"text": "Mrs. Hanh yanked off the blanket. A breeze hit my neck. Whoosh."
},
{
"t": 188.21,
"dur": 7.304,
"text": "My head snapped back into place. I sat up and stretched my neck. Tung fainted. Three hundred thousand people applauded."
},
{
"t": 196.314,
"dur": 8.058,
"text": "That clip has thirty million views now. Nobody believes it's real. Good. If they don't believe, I can still sneak out for a late meal."
},
{
"t": 204.621,
"dur": 6.266,
"text": "He paid off his debts. He still sets up the camera at dinner. But when he turns it off, he sits and eats with me."
},
{
"t": 211.137,
"dur": 1.741,
"text": "And I gave him a piece of paper."
},
{
"t": 215.828,
"dur": 10.42,
"text": "Fifty years as a ma lai, and she never scared anyone. Three months online, and she's got a revenue deal. I've sat on cabinets for centuries. Nobody's paid me a dime."
},
{
"t": 226.498,
"dur": 7.088,
"text": "Next time: an underworld clerk shows up at a sewing shop to take attendance, and marks exactly one person wrong."
},
{
"t": 233.835,
"dur": 3.654,
"text": "Hit subscribe. Or tonight I'll be sitting on top of your cabinet."
}
],
